    <node id="&quot;FEZZIWIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fezziwig is a character who is known for dancing joyfully with his wife, Mrs. Fezziwig, and hosting festive gatherings during Christmas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fezziwig is a jovial old gentleman and former employer of Scrooge, remembered fondly for his kind and lively character."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fezziwig is portrayed as a jovial and generous figure, responsible for organizing joyful gatherings and fostering a sense of community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fezziwig is portrayed as a jovial figure who hosts a lively domestic ball, engaging with guests and spreading cheer during the event."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2f98bc7abb0c67d4c86055c7fd72218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc1edd983869352d14cf0886a9175a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c248858d1b13ab7ee9ca13c1aeed6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMBUG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humbug reflects Scrooge's initial skepticism towards the supernatural and his reluctance to accept the warnings he receives."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE COMMON WELFARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Common Welfare refers to the overarching principle of caring for others, emphasizing charity, mercy, and benevolence as essential values."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE EARTHLY WORLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The earthly world contrasts with the spectral realm, illustrating Scrooge's struggles between materialism and moral reckoning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRISTMAS DINNER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Christmas Dinner is a gathering where the Cratchit family enjoys a meal together, highlighting themes of unity and celebration in their humble circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Christmas Dinner is the meal that the Cratchit family prepares and eagerly awaits, representing a time of unity and festivity despite their financial struggles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4b58de5429cd1261370c231c8673e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503f0bfa5453467c7c61d160a3540eca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALTERED SPIRIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Altered Spirit signifies the changes one undergoes internally and how it affects relationships and personal aspirations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54bdd22db1f84a965b5f4c06c9216d8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIRM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The firm, known as Scrooge and Marley, is a business partnership that has existed for many years between Scrooge and Marley."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CLOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Clock is an object that signifies the passage of time, marking the hours that are relevant to Scrooge's supernatural encounters."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Clock is referenced as a device that fails to keep accurate time, symbolizing Scrooge's disorientation and confusion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b10789a9cb0af6c553730b29bd9034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRISTMAS EVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Christmas Eves serve as a time marker in the story, representing the passage of time and the reflections on one’s life and actions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JACOB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jacob was Scrooge's old business partner, whose recent death prompts reflections on life and death during the story."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CREDENTIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Credentials refer to the documents presented by The Gentlemen to establish their authority and request financial contributions for the needy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANOTHER ATMOSPHERE OF LIFE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Another Atmosphere of Life suggests a transformative environment or state of being that influences one's feelings and outlook on life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54bdd22db1f84a965b5f4c06c9216d8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. FEZZIWIG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mrs. Fezziwig is depicted as a partner to Fezziwig, participating in the social dance and contributing to the joyful atmosphere."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Fezziwig is mentioned as a significant partner to Fezziwig, contributing to the festive atmosphere of the gatherings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Fezziwig is the partner of Mr. Fezziwig, contributing to their spirit of joy during the festive season."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mrs. Fezziwig is the wife of Fezziwig, who participates joyfully in the Christmas dances, showcasing the festive spirit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2f98bc7abb0c67d4c86055c7fd72218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc1edd983869352d14cf0886a9175a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CHIMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chimes indicate the time and create a rhythm that sets the stage for Scrooge's awakening and realization of time's flow."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPIRITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spirits refer to supernatural beings that exist beyond physical life, serving as a representation of human consciousness and the afterlife."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CLERK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Clerk is an employee in Scrooge's office who shows a warmer disposition towards Christmas compared to Scrooge."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Clerk is an unnamed employee working under Scrooge, who endures Scrooge's harsh attitude while showcasing a polite demeanor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Clerk works in Scrooge's Counting-House, portrayed as being under Scrooge's cold and uninviting employment conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2466de2f67fd710ef2f20c0a8d9e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9aac3484185ac66045df92214d245d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE PHANTOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Phantom represents a fearful and silent presence that embodies the unknown consequences of Scrooge's life choices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Phantom represents a ghostly figure guiding Scrooge through reflections on his past, present, and future."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-02baee20cc9463dbe08170a8e1043e32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEMORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Memory encapsulates the recollections of the past that influence current emotions and decisions, playing a pivotal role in Scrooge's narrative."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54bdd22db1f84a965b5f4c06c9216d8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joe is a character who engages in conversation about taking down bed-curtains, providing a humorous perspective on the situation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joe is a marine-store dealer who is involved in the more unsavory elements of society, showing the contrast between Scrooge and other characters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Joe is an old character who engages in a conversation about the belongings of a deceased man, exhibiting a cynical attitude towards the situation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f29eeadc1d8ab46dc8a0bbd3c56b64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE WRAPPER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Wrapper is an item associated with the Ghost, symbolizing its ethereal nature and connection to the afterlife."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The chain symbolizes the burden of one's past actions and choices, illustrating how they can weigh heavily on the spirit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MR. MARLEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mr. Marley is referenced as Scrooge's deceased business partner, whose death has significant implications for Scrooge's character and outlook."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Town is the setting of the events, representing a community coming together to celebrate Christmas and engage in holiday traditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Town refers to the setting where Scrooge resides, characterized by a mix of busy and obscure areas, and reflects themes of socioeconomic disparity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0f459f5af1c3a5e0b92cbe4ee48b77b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMFORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Comfort refers to the emotional warmth and contentment associated with family and home, which is lacking in Scrooge's life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54bdd22db1f84a965b5f4c06c9216d8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLD SCRATCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Old Scratch is a colloquial reference to the devil or an evil spirit, mentioned in a light-hearted exchange between characters."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89777b838d5447c7bd1ec11282c4ee89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARY'S GHOST IN WHITE WAISTCOAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mary's Ghost in White Waistcoat is mentioned as a familiar spirit associated with Scrooge, symbolizing past connections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONEY-CHANGING HOLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The money-changing hole refers to the narrow focus of Scrooge's life on financial gain, contrasting with broader human concerns."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHRISTMAS-TIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Christmas-time encompasses the entire holiday season, marked by various traditions and social expectations surrounding generosity and joy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Christmas-time refers to the festive period during which the events of the text take place, highlighting themes of celebration and reunion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6c248858d1b13ab7ee9ca13c1aeed6b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUSINESSMEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Businessmen are depicted as wealthy individuals who engage in trivial conversations, highlighting their preoccupation with business over personal connections."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHILDHOOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Childhood symbolizes innocence, joy, and the simplicity of life, aspects that Scrooge longs for as he reflects on his past."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54bdd22db1f84a965b5f4c06c9216d8d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bob is an implied character in the text whose situation becomes a point of humor related to Scrooge's pranks or gifts."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f738cb25d60a7dab782162d9d0a25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CLOCKWORKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Clockworks alludes to the mechanisms governing time, metaphorically connected to Scrooge's experiences during the haunting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb661c37436355ccec2769b1d0350c5f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE BLESSED STAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Blessed Star symbolizes guidance and hope, referring to the star that led the Wise Men and representing moral direction."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE DYING FLAME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The dying flame represents the fading warmth and life, a metaphor for Scrooge's cold-hearted nature and the impending notions of death."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE LOW-BROWED SHOP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Low-browed Shop is a degraded establishment where various refuse and old items are traded, illustrating the grim realities of the town."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GHOST OF CHRISTMAS PAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ghost of Christmas Past is a spectral being guiding Scrooge through his memories, representing reflection and reclamation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Ghost of Christmas Past is a spirit that shows Scrooge his past, illustrating the experiences that shaped his current demeanor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb21d58d36c6306fd8810ddd51c4a971&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAMDEN TOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Camden Town is a location referenced in the text, indicating where Bob Cratchit runs home to celebrate Christmas Eve with his family."&lt;SEP&gt;"Camden Town is mentioned as a location, indicating the logistical challenges associated with delivering a large turkey."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f738cb25d60a7dab782162d9d0a25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9aac3484185ac66045df92214d245d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE CHIME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chime is described as a significant auditory cue in the narrative, marking the passage of time and heralding the arrival of the Ghost."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b10789a9cb0af6c553730b29bd9034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MANKIND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mankind encompasses all humans and emphasizes the interconnectedness and responsibilities individuals have toward one another."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-359187e7571bda4b0b08b2e0b6581e52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SEASON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Season refers to the broader context of the Christmas period, emphasizing cultural practices of generosity and connection among people."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5dac41b3f9eeaf794f0147400b1718cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RED-FACED GENTLEMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Red-faced Gentleman engages in conversation, displaying frustration and contributing to the atmosphere of casual disregard for the deceased."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARKET-TOWN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Market-town is a setting in Scrooge's past where he recalls joyous memories, symbolizing his childhood experiences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb21d58d36c6306fd8810ddd51c4a971</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE POULTERER'S MAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The poulterer's man is a character mentioned in relation to delivering a turkey, highlighting the importance of feasting during the Christmas season."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f738cb25d60a7dab782162d9d0a25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EBENEZER SCROOGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ebenezer Scrooge is a central character, depicted as reflecting on his past, particularly his relationship with Dick Wilkins and his former self."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ebenezer Scrooge is the central character who grapples with a profound existential crisis, experiencing confusion about time and visiting from the supernatural."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ebenezer Scrooge is the main character of 'A Christmas Carol', depicted as a miserly and transformed figure through encounters with spirits during Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b10789a9cb0af6c553730b29bd9034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e3921da66da5d761ab73cd849af6c43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bc1edd983869352d14cf0886a9175a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE WOMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Woman participates in the dialogue with Joe, displaying a sense of humor and practicality about the deceased man's possessions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f29eeadc1d8ab46dc8a0bbd3c56b64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTLEMAN WITH THE EXCRESCENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Gentleman with the excrescence on his nose is characterized by his humor and self-deprecating remarks regarding funeral attendance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The City is a general reference within the text, symbolizing the broader society that observes Scrooge’s transformation and embodies the societal norms and values of the time."&lt;SEP&gt;"The City represents an urban environment bustling with activity, highlighted during the Christmas season."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6c248858d1b13ab7ee9ca13c1aeed6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bea83e7153fc2064aa382b494936a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MERRY CHRISTMAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Merry Christmas is a phrase used by Mr. and Mrs. Fezziwig to convey goodwill and festive spirit to their guests as they leave the ball."&lt;SEP&gt;"Merry Christmas represents a recurring theme in Scrooge's reflections, signifying joy and celebration that he struggles to connect with."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b2f98bc7abb0c67d4c86055c7fd72218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb21d58d36c6306fd8810ddd51c4a971</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE TURKEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The turkey is a central focus of Scrooge's joy and generosity, symbolizing abundance and the spirit of giving during Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f738cb25d60a7dab782162d9d0a25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;A CHILD/OLD MAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The figure’s appearance, resembling a blend of a child and an old man, symbolizes the complexity of time and the paradoxes Scrooge faces in understanding his life."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b10789a9cb0af6c553730b29bd9034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE DECEASED MAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Deceased Man is discussed throughout the dialogue as a subject of disdain and mockery among Joe and The Woman."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f29eeadc1d8ab46dc8a0bbd3c56b64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE INFERNAL ATMOSPHERE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The infernal atmosphere surrounding Marley's Ghost highlights the chilling effect of guilt and the consequences of denying one's humanity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1aa50206d02ed89418f65f97c6441d1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNERAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Funeral referenced implies the death of Jacob and the social implications surrounding it, including indifferent attitudes from acquaintances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The School is a location from Scrooge's childhood where he recalls feeling neglected and alone, impacting his character development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The School is a setting in the story where a solitary child is left, symbolizing neglect and abandonment during Christmas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8590d9263cd2cd4fa583c432fc54e6c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb21d58d36c6306fd8810ddd51c4a971</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE STREETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The streets are the setting for Scrooge's joyful exploration and transformation, indicating his engagement with the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f738cb25d60a7dab782162d9d0a25ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WINTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Winter serves as a backdrop in the narrative, emphasizing the coldness of Scrooge's heart and the bleakness of his existence before transformation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b10789a9cb0af6c553730b29bd9034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BED-CURTAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CATEGORY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bed-curtains are discussed as items of possession taken down from the deceased man's bed, illustrating a lack of respect and a practical approach to his belongings."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f29eeadc1d8ab46dc8a0bbd3c56b64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLUMP SISTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Plump Sister is another family member at the gathering, representing the jovial and welcoming atmosphere of the Christmas celebration."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-94bea83e7153fc2064aa382b494936a1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THE STREET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GEO"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Street represents the location where Scrooge observes people and gatherings, highlighting the social interactions typical of the town."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1a4fbcf1ed86864b9bfd5e8dba4c683</data>
